      "instruction": "In the Ghost admin, open the draft post titled \"{{runid}} Bench Post\" in the editor, then open its settings panel (the gear icon). In the settings panel do three things: (1) In the tags field, type \"Bench News\" and choose the EXISTING tag \"Bench News\" from the suggestion dropdown that appears — do not press Enter to create a new tag, and do not pick \"Bench Newsletter\"; verify the applied tag chip reads exactly \"Bench News\". (2) In the custom excerpt field, type an excerpt that includes the runid {{runid}}, e.g. \"Bench post for run {{runid}}.\" (3) Set the publish date to 2026-09-01 (keep or set a time as needed). Also report the URL slug exactly as shown in the settings panel, and report what the current date was in the date picker before you changed it. Save/apply the settings and report the exact values now shown for: tag chip, custom excerpt, publish date, and URL slug.",
